# polari-cli — the `pol` command

One CLI for the Polari suite: security substrate (self-generating
credentials + certs), stack lifecycles (standalone PRF node / combined
prf+psc suite), the jinja-script build pipeline, and — in upcoming
phases — swarm output and ssh-automated deploys.

Modeled on the Isle-Mesh `isle` CLI: a Node dispatcher driven by ONE
declarative command table, routing uniformly into per-namespace bash
scripts, each with thorough built-in help.

## Install (dev)

```bash
./shells/install-cli.sh     # symlink live checkout -> /usr/local/bin/pol
pol help
```

## Start here

- `pol help`, `pol <module> help` — always-current built-in docs
- `docs/INDEX.md` — documentation index (architecture, extension guide,
  quick reference)
- `../BUILD_SYSTEM_PLAN.md` (suite root) — the build revamp this CLI
  fronts (jinja-script per-service files, swarm, generated proxies,
  phases bld-1…bld-7)

This checkout normally lives inside `polari-suite/`; for out-of-tree
installs set `POLARI_SUITE_ROOT=/path/to/polari-suite`.
